    # activateAnimationKeyframe (s98, 16th crash class): SIGBUS, unguarded
    # table-lookup-then-dereference. arg_r4 (an animation/keyframe index)
    # indexes a fixed pointer table at 0x8009FC10 with no bounds check, and
    # whatever comes out (ctx->r17) is immediately dereferenced at +0x30 --
    # same "unguarded-pointer-off-a-lookup" signature as the rest of the
    # hangar-tick family, but this is the first one of that family getting a
    # guard instead of just an entry log (per s98/NEXT.md's pivot -- 4
    # straight sessions of log-only instruments each found a different new
    # crash and never converged). ctx->r17 is used pervasively as a base
    # pointer for the rest of the function body (MEM_BU(ctx->r17, 0x1F),
    # ADD32(ctx->r17, ctx->r16), etc.), so a partial guard (default only the
    # +0x30 deref) would still crash later in the same function on the same
    # bad pointer. A bare `return;` is NOT safe either: the prologue spills
    # s0-s3/ra to the guest stack (MEM_W at sp+0x10/0x14/0x18/0x1c/0x20) and
    # the real epilogue at L_80061F18 (also the existing "not found" bail
