    # arg-pointer deref (9th/10th/11th class), but an unbounded
    # pointer-chasing loop with zero validation on the chased pointer at
    # any step. If the node findAndUnlinkSmallestEntry returns is corrupt,
    # or any node's own first field ("next") is corrupt, the very next
    # iteration walks off into unmapped memory -- matching the crash PC
    # exactly (0x80010174 is the loop's own dereference instruction).
    # The pre-existing code already has a ready-made "abandon this relink,
    # nothing to see here" reentry point at L_800101A4 (used at 0x80010160
    # when the initial pointer is null) that reloads its one live register
    # (a0) fresh from a global head pointer at 0x801163B0 -- it does not
    # depend on anything computed inside the loop, so it is safe to jump to
    # from mid-loop too, same degrade-to-empty-list semantics the original
    # code already uses for the null-pointer case. Guard checks $v1
    # (ctx->r3) for RDRAM-range sanity at the top of every loop iteration
