    # s230: render-cache "epoch" diagnostic. s225/s226/s229 proved the
    # traverseSceneGraphRecursive->processSceneNode->submitSceneNodeRender
    # call chain AND the camera struct's own data (m00, deref0) keep
    # changing throughout the picture-freeze window, so the wedge is
    # neither "stopped running" nor "stopped updating" -- something
    # produces identical output despite live input. A read-only source
    # trace of processSceneNode/submitSceneNodeRender (funcs_4.c) this
    # session found: submitSceneNodeRender reads a global word at fixed
    # RDRAM 0x8011A894 (funcs_4.c:10-12, lui 0x8012 / -0x576C) and
    # unconditionally stamps it into MEM_W(node_ptr+0x30) every call
    # (funcs_4.c:41-42); processSceneNode has two near-identical
