    # near-duplicate branches, ten call sites total), and those callees are
    # too large (up to ~5000 lines) to manually re-derive from source this
    # session, this is NEXT.md's bounded per-call counter/log fallback: a
    # tracer (NOT a guard -- no skip, no behavior change) at each of the ten
    # call sites, logging the two pointer args (a0/ctx->r4, a2/ctx->r6) each
    # site actually passes in immediately before the call. Two things this
    # narrows: (1) if the args are already non-canonical (top 32 bits !=
    # 0xFFFFFFFF) AT THE CALL SITE, the corruption predates the callee and
    # this source-read conclusion needs revisiting; (2) regardless, the LAST
