    # discipline the s436 "type-c" 7-site -0x63B0 patch, the s251
    # DLENTRY_TAIL_GUARD sites list, and the S392/S393 audits all used for
    # non-byte-identical idiom instances. Each site's own address doubles as
    # a globally-unique tag, so no cross-site variable-name collision is
    # possible even where multiple sites share one function (up to 22, in
    # renderLitMeshFaceGroup) -- each patched block is its own `{ }` scope,
    # matching DL_LIST_APPEND_GUARD's own precedent for this.
    #
    # Remediation: "skip the write, nothing downstream depends on it
    # happening" -- the same precedent as DL_LIST_APPEND_GUARD/
    # FREELIST_NEXT_GUARD (a field store here has no in-function consumer of
    # its own success; unlike a 2nd-hop deref, there's nothing further to
    # protect once the write itself is skipped). Two functions in this list
